course: dictionary
lesson: 14447
title: Paperback and hardback
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A paperback is a book with a soft cover made of thick paper. The word is made of two parts, paper and back, and it tells you what the cover is made of. «I read my paperback on the bus.» Here the paperback is the book in Ellie's hands.
explain: Books can also have a hard cover. That kind is called a hardback. «The shop sells the hardback for twelve pounds and the paperback for six.» The sentence gives you clues: the two books have different prices, and the paperback is the cheaper one.
explain: Paperback can also describe a book. When it comes before a noun, it is an adjective. «The library has a paperback edition of the story.» Here paperback tells you what kind of edition it is.
fact: A paperback is a book with a soft cover made of thick paper.
fact: A hardback is a book with a hard cover.
fact: Paperbacks are usually cheaper and lighter than hardbacks, so they are easy to carry in a bag.
fact: «Paperback» can be a noun, as in «a paperback», or an adjective, as in «a paperback book».
fact: The phrase «in paperback» means the book is published with a soft cover.
exercise: «The paperback was cheap, so Mia bought it.» What is a paperback? | A short story printed on a card | A map of the library | *A book with a soft cover made of thick paper | A book with a hard cover
exercise: The hardback costs £12 and the paperback costs £6. Which price is the paperback? | £18 | £4 | *£6 | £12
exercise: In «the paperback edition», what kind of word is paperback? | A verb, an action word | A noun for a person | A number | *An adjective, a word that describes the edition
test: Which book is usually lighter to carry in your bag? | The big dictionary | The atlas | *The paperback | The hardback
test: What does «the paperback edition» of a book mean? | A version written in capital letters | A version with no pages | A version with a hard cover | *A version with a soft cover made of thick paper
exam: «The paperback was cheaper than the hardback, so Sam chose it.» Why did Sam choose the paperback? | *It was cheaper | It had more pages | It was written in French | It was bigger
